  ('GK-0186', 'Everyday science', 'Earth and space', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: General Science textbooks (Punjab Textbook Board, classes 9-10)', 'The true shape of the Earth is best described as a:', '["Geoid", "Perfect sphere", "Cube", "Cylinder"]', 0, 'The Earth is slightly flattened at the poles; its true shape is called a geoid.', '{"1": "The Earth bulges at the equator.", "2": "The Earth is round.", "3": "The Earth is round."}'),
  ('GK-0187', 'Everyday science', 'Earth and space', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: International Astronomical Union', 'How many planets are in the Solar System?', '["Nine", "Seven", "Eight", "Ten"]', 2, 'Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune.', '{"0": "Pluto was reclassified as a dwarf planet in 2006.", "1": "There are eight.", "3": "There are eight."}'),
  ('GK-0188', 'Everyday science', 'Earth and space', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: Encyclopaedia Britannica', 'The Big Bang theory of the origin of the universe was first proposed by:', '["Isaac Newton", "Georges Lemaître", "Edwin Hubble", "Galileo Galilei"]', 1, 'Belgian priest-physicist Georges Lemaître proposed the ''primeval atom'' idea in 1927–1931.', '{"0": "Newton gave the law of gravitation.", "2": "Hubble showed galaxies are moving apart.", "3": "Galileo used the telescope."}'),
  ('GK-0189', 'Everyday science', 'Biology and health', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: World Health Organization', 'Dengue fever is caused by a:', '["Virus", "Bacterium", "Fungus", "Plasmodium parasite"]', 0, 'Dengue is a virus spread by the Aedes mosquito.', '{"1": "Dengue is not bacterial.", "2": "Dengue is not fungal.", "3": "Plasmodium causes malaria."}'),
  ('GK-0190', 'Everyday science', 'Biology and health', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: General Science textbooks (Punjab Textbook Board, classes 9-10)', 'Anaemia is a disorder of the:', '["Skin", "Blood", "Brain", "Lungs"]', 1, 'Anaemia means too few red blood cells or too little haemoglobin.', '{"0": "Skin disorders include eczema.", "2": "Brain disorders include epilepsy.", "3": "Lung disorders include asthma."}'),
  ('GK-0191', 'Everyday science', 'Biology and health', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: General Science textbooks (Punjab Textbook Board, classes 9-10)', 'A doctor who treats skin diseases is a:', '["Endocrinologist", "Cardiologist", "Dermatologist", "Neurologist"]', 2, 'Dermatology is the branch of medicine dealing with skin.', '{"0": "An endocrinologist treats hormone glands.", "1": "A cardiologist treats the heart.", "3": "A neurologist treats the nervous system."}'),
  ('GK-0192', 'Everyday science', 'Biology and health', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: General Science textbooks (Punjab Textbook Board, classes 9-10)', 'Ornithology is the study of:', '["Birds", "Insects", "Snakes", "Fish"]', 0, 'Ornithology is the scientific study of birds.', '{"1": "Insects are studied in entomology.", "2": "Reptiles are studied in herpetology.", "3": "Fish are studied in ichthyology."}'),
  ('GK-0193', 'Everyday science', 'Biology and health', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: General Science textbooks (Punjab Textbook Board, classes 9-10)', 'Insomnia means:', '["Colour blindness", "Loss of memory", "Inability to sleep", "Fear of heights"]', 2, 'Insomnia is long-term difficulty in falling or staying asleep.', '{"0": "Colour blindness is a defect of vision.", "1": "Loss of memory is amnesia.", "3": "Fear of heights is acrophobia."}'),
  ('GK-0194', 'Everyday science', 'Biology and health', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: General Science textbooks (Punjab Textbook Board, classes 9-10)', 'Claustrophobia is the fear of:', '["Crowds", "Closed spaces", "Heights", "Water"]', 1, 'Claustrophobia is an intense fear of small or enclosed spaces.', '{"0": "Fear of crowded places is agoraphobia.", "2": "Fear of heights is acrophobia.", "3": "Fear of water is aquaphobia."}'),
  ('GK-0195', 'Everyday science', 'Biology and health', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: General Science textbooks (Punjab Textbook Board, classes 9-10)', 'Lacrimal glands produce:', '["Tears", "Saliva", "Bile", "Insulin"]', 0, 'The lacrimal glands above each eye make tears.', '{"1": "Saliva comes from the salivary glands.", "2": "Bile comes from the liver.", "3": "Insulin comes from the pancreas."}'),
  ('GK-0196', 'Everyday science', 'Biology and health', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: Encyclopaedia Britannica', 'The word ''vitamine'' was coined in 1912 by:', '["Louis Pasteur", "Casimir Funk", "Robert Koch", "Alexander Fleming"]', 1, 'Polish biochemist Casimir Funk coined ''vitamine'' (vital amine).', '{"0": "Pasteur worked on germs and vaccines.", "2": "Koch discovered the TB germ.", "3": "Fleming discovered penicillin."}'),
  ('GK-0197', 'Everyday science', 'Biology and health', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: General Science textbooks (Punjab Textbook Board, classes 9-10)', 'The largest mammal in the world is the:', '["Giraffe", "African elephant", "Blue whale", "Whale shark"]', 2, 'The blue whale is the largest animal ever known.', '{"0": "The giraffe is the tallest animal.", "1": "The elephant is the largest land animal.", "3": "The whale shark is a fish, not a mammal."}'),
  ('GK-0198', 'Everyday science', 'Biology and health', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: Encyclopaedia Britannica', 'Which animal cannot stick out its tongue?', '["Crocodile", "Giraffe", "Snake", "Frog"]', 0, 'A crocodile''s tongue is held to the floor of its mouth by a membrane.', '{"1": "Giraffes use long tongues to strip leaves.", "2": "Snakes flick their tongues out constantly.", "3": "Frogs shoot their tongues out to catch insects."}'),
  ('GK-0199', 'Everyday science', 'Chemistry', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: General Science textbooks (Punjab Textbook Board, classes 9-10)', 'The acid used in car batteries is:', '["Nitric acid", "Sulphuric acid", "Citric acid", "Hydrochloric acid"]', 1, 'Lead–acid car batteries use dilute sulphuric acid.', '{"0": "Nitric acid is used for fertilisers and explosives.", "2": "Citric acid is in lemons.", "3": "Hydrochloric acid is in the stomach."}'),
  ('GK-0200', 'Everyday science', 'Chemistry', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: IPCC', 'The main gas causing global warming is:', '["Oxygen", "Nitrogen", "Carbon dioxide", "Hydrogen"]', 2, 'Carbon dioxide from burning fuel is the largest cause of human-made warming.', '{"0": "Oxygen is not a greenhouse gas.", "1": "Nitrogen is not a greenhouse gas.", "3": "Hydrogen is not a greenhouse gas."}'),
  ('GK-0201', 'Everyday science', 'Chemistry', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: General Science textbooks (Punjab Textbook Board, classes 9-10)', 'Horticulture is the growing of:', '["Fruits, vegetables and flowers", "Silkworms", "Cereal crops only", "Fish"]', 0, 'Horticulture is garden cultivation of fruits, vegetables and flowers.', '{"1": "That is sericulture.", "2": "Cereals belong to agronomy.", "3": "That is pisciculture."}'),
  ('GK-0202', 'Famous people, books and firsts', 'Books', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: Encyclopaedia Britannica', '''A Brief History of Time'' was written by:', '["Stephen Hawking", "Richard Dawkins", "Albert Einstein", "Carl Sagan"]', 0, 'Physicist Stephen Hawking published ''A Brief History of Time'' in 1988.', '{"1": "Dawkins wrote ''The Selfish Gene''.", "2": "Einstein did not write this book.", "3": "Sagan wrote ''Cosmos''."}'),
  ('GK-0203', 'Famous people, books and firsts', 'Books', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: Encyclopaedia Britannica', '''A Tale of Two Cities'' was written by:', '["Thomas Hardy", "Charles Dickens", "Leo Tolstoy", "Jane Austen"]', 1, 'Dickens''s 1859 novel is set in London and Paris during the French Revolution.', '{"0": "Hardy wrote ''Tess of the d''Urbervilles''.", "2": "Tolstoy wrote ''War and Peace''.", "3": "Austen wrote ''Pride and Prejudice''."}'),
  ('GK-0204', 'Famous people, books and firsts', 'Books', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: Encyclopaedia Britannica', '''The Clash of Civilizations'' theory was put forward by:', '["Henry Kissinger", "Francis Fukuyama", "Samuel P. Huntington", "Noam Chomsky"]', 2, 'Huntington argued that future conflicts would be between cultures (1993 article, 1996 book).', '{"0": "Kissinger wrote ''Diplomacy''.", "1": "Fukuyama wrote ''The End of History''.", "3": "Chomsky is a linguist and critic."}'),
  ('GK-0205', 'Famous people, books and firsts', 'Books', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, General Knowledge. Checked against: Encyclopaedia Britannica', '''The Godfather'' was written by:', '["Victor Hugo", "Mario Puzo", "John Grisham", "Ernest Hemingway"]', 1, 'Mario Puzo''s 1969 novel was made into a famous film.', '{"0": "Hugo wrote ''Les Misérables''.", "2": "Grisham writes legal thrillers.", "3": "Hemingway wrote ''The Old Man and the Sea''."}')
