  ('PST-0268', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Deserts', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'The Thar Desert in Pakistan lies mainly in:', '["Gilgit-Baltistan", "Sindh", "Balochistan", "Khyber Pakhtunkhwa"]', 1, 'The Thar Desert spreads over south-eastern Sindh (Tharparkar) and Rajasthan in India.', '{"0": "Gilgit-Baltistan has a cold desert near Skardu.", "2": "Balochistan has the Kharan Desert.", "3": "KP has no part of the Thar."}'),
  ('PST-0269', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Dams and barrages', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'Warsak Dam is built on the:', '["Swat River", "Jhelum", "Indus", "Kabul River"]', 3, 'Warsak Dam, near Peshawar, is on the Kabul River.', '{"0": "Swat has Munda Dam (planned).", "1": "Mangla is on the Jhelum.", "2": "Tarbela is on the Indus."}'),
