  ('PST-0271', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Dams and barrages', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'Tarbela Dam was completed in:', '["1976", "2004", "1960", "1967"]', 0, 'Tarbela, one of the largest earth-filled dams in the world, was completed in 1976.', '{"1": "2004 is Ghazi Barotha.", "2": "1960 is the Indus Waters Treaty.", "3": "1967 is when Mangla Dam was completed."}'),
  ('PST-0272', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Dams and barrages', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'Jinnah Barrage on the Indus is near:', '["Taunsa", "Kalabagh, Mianwali", "Sukkur", "Hyderabad"]', 1, 'Jinnah Barrage, completed in 1946, is near Kalabagh in Mianwali district.', '{"0": "Taunsa has its own barrage.", "2": "Sukkur has the Lloyd Barrage.", "3": "Kotri Barrage is near Hyderabad."}'),
  ('PST-0273', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Dams and barrages', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'Gomal Zam Dam is built on the:', '["Gomal River", "Swat River", "Kabul River", "Kurram River"]', 0, 'Gomal Zam Dam is in South Waziristan on the Gomal River.', '{"1": "Swat is in Malakand.", "2": "Warsak is on the Kabul River.", "3": "Kurram has its own projects."}'),
  ('PST-0274', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Ports', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Economic Survey; Pakistan Studies (compulsory), PTB', 'Pakistan''s second biggest seaport is:', '["Pasni", "Gwadar", "Ormara", "Port Qasim"]', 3, 'Port Muhammad bin Qasim near Karachi is the second busiest port after Karachi Port.', '{"0": "Pasni is a fishing harbour.", "1": "Gwadar is newer and smaller in trade.", "2": "Ormara is a naval base."}'),
  ('PST-0275', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Ports', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Economic Survey; Pakistan Studies (compulsory), PTB', 'Sost, a dry port on the China border, is in:', '["Balochistan", "Punjab", "Khyber Pakhtunkhwa", "Gilgit-Baltistan"]', 3, 'Sost, in upper Hunza, handles trade over the Khunjerab Pass.', '{"0": "Balochistan''s border points include Taftan and Chaman.", "1": "Punjab''s dry ports include Lahore and Sialkot.", "2": "KP''s dry ports include Peshawar."}'),
  ('PST-0276', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Roads', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Economic Survey; Pakistan Studies (compulsory), PTB', 'The Karakoram Highway (N-35) is also known as the:', '["Friendship Highway", "Grand Trunk Road", "Indus Highway", "Makran Coastal Highway"]', 0, 'The KKH was built with China and links Hasan Abdal to the Khunjerab Pass.', '{"1": "The GT Road is N-5.", "2": "That is N-55.", "3": "That is N-10."}'),
  ('PST-0277', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Roads', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Economic Survey; Pakistan Studies (compulsory), PTB', 'The M-2 motorway connects:', '["Karachi and Hyderabad", "Islamabad and Lahore", "Lahore and Multan", "Islamabad and Peshawar"]', 1, 'The M-2, opened in 1997, was Pakistan''s first motorway.', '{"0": "That is the M-9.", "2": "That is part of the M-3/M-4 network.", "3": "That is the M-1."}'),
  ('PST-0278', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Cities', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'Quetta was once called:', '["Shalkot", "Lyallpur", "Campbellpur", "Neroon Kot"]', 0, 'Quetta''s old name was Shalkot.', '{"1": "Lyallpur is Faisalabad.", "2": "Campbellpur is Attock.", "3": "Neroon Kot is Hyderabad."}'),
  ('PST-0279', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Cities', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'Attock was formerly called:', '["Ajodhan", "Montgomery", "Campbellpur", "Shalkot"]', 2, 'Attock district was named Campbellpur under British rule.', '{"0": "Ajodhan is Pakpattan.", "1": "Montgomery is Sahiwal.", "3": "Shalkot is Quetta."}'),
  ('PST-0280', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Cities', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'Pakpattan was formerly known as:', '["Neroon Kot", "Khangarh", "Ajodhan", "Shalkot"]', 2, 'Ajodhan was renamed Pakpattan after Baba Farid Ganj Shakar settled there.', '{"0": "Neroon Kot is Hyderabad.", "1": "Khangarh is Jacobabad.", "3": "Shalkot is Quetta."}'),
  ('PST-0281', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Cities', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'Hyderabad (Sindh) was once called:', '["Ajodhan", "Neroon Kot", "Shalkot", "Campbellpur"]', 1, 'The Kalhoras founded Hyderabad in 1768 on the site of Neroon Kot.', '{"0": "Ajodhan is Pakpattan.", "2": "Shalkot is Quetta.", "3": "Campbellpur is Attock."}'),
  ('PST-0282', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Cities', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'Which city is called the ''Manchester of Pakistan'' for its textile industry?', '["Gujranwala", "Faisalabad", "Multan", "Sialkot"]', 1, 'Faisalabad is Pakistan''s main textile centre.', '{"0": "Gujranwala is famous for metal goods.", "2": "Multan is the city of saints.", "3": "Sialkot is famous for sports goods."}'),
  ('PST-0283', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Cities', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'Which city is known as the ''City of Saints''?', '["Multan", "Peshawar", "Lahore", "Karachi"]', 0, 'Multan has many famous shrines, including Bahauddin Zakariya and Shah Rukn-e-Alam.', '{"1": "Peshawar is called the city of flowers.", "2": "Lahore is called the city of gardens.", "3": "Karachi is called the city of lights."}'),
  ('PST-0284', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Cities', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Economic Survey; Pakistan Studies (compulsory), PTB', 'Sialkot is world-famous for making:', '["Steel", "Sports goods and surgical instruments", "Textiles", "Carpets"]', 1, 'Sialkot makes footballs used worldwide, as well as surgical instruments.', '{"0": "Karachi has Pakistan Steel.", "2": "Faisalabad is the textile centre.", "3": "Carpets are made in many cities, not mainly Sialkot."}'),
  ('PST-0285', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Cities', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'Which valley is called the ''Switzerland of Pakistan''?', '["Hunza", "Neelum", "Swat", "Kaghan"]', 2, 'Swat is known as the Switzerland of Pakistan for its scenery.', '{"0": "Hunza is famous for apricots and long life.", "1": "Neelum is in Azad Kashmir.", "3": "Kaghan is famous for Lake Saiful Muluk."}'),
  ('PST-0286', 'Geography of Pakistan', 'Cities', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Geography, Economy and People (Fazle Karim Khan); Pakistan Bureau of Statistics', 'The Hiran Minar, built by Emperor Jahangir, is near:', '["Multan", "Thatta", "Sheikhupura", "Attock"]', 2, 'Jahangir built Hiran Minar near Sheikhupura in memory of his pet deer.', '{"0": "Multan has the shrines.", "1": "Thatta has the Shah Jahan Mosque.", "3": "Attock has Attock Fort."}')
