  ('PST-0300', 'Economy, resources and culture', 'Culture', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Economic Survey; Pakistan Studies (compulsory), PTB', 'The Sufi poet Bulleh Shah is buried at:', '["Kasur", "Jhang", "Pakpattan", "Bhit Shah"]', 0, 'Bulleh Shah (died 1757) is buried in Kasur.', '{"1": "Jhang is linked to Heer.", "2": "Baba Farid is buried at Pakpattan.", "3": "Shah Abdul Latif is buried at Bhit Shah."}'),
  ('PST-0301', 'Economy, resources and culture', 'Culture', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Economic Survey; Pakistan Studies (compulsory), PTB', 'Who is regarded as the first great poet of the Punjabi language?', '["Bulleh Shah", "Baba Farid Ganj Shakar", "Waris Shah", "Mian Muhammad Bakhsh"]', 1, 'Baba Farid (12th–13th century) wrote the earliest Punjabi verse that survives.', '{"0": "Bulleh Shah lived in the 17th–18th century.", "2": "Waris Shah wrote Heer in the 18th century.", "3": "He wrote Saif-ul-Muluk in the 19th century."}'),
  ('PST-0302', 'Economy, resources and culture', 'Culture', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Economic Survey; Pakistan Studies (compulsory), PTB', 'The famous painter Abdur Rahman Chughtai is known for:', '["Calligraphy only", "Architecture", "Music", "Painting"]', 3, 'Abdur Rahman Chughtai (1894–1975) developed a distinctive Mughal-inspired painting style.', '{"0": "He is known mainly as a painter.", "1": "A famous architect is Nayyar Ali Dada.", "2": "Famous musicians include Nusrat Fateh Ali Khan."}'),
  ('PST-0303', 'Economy, resources and culture', 'Culture', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: S. M. Ikram, Muslim Civilization in India; Pakistan Studies (compulsory), PTB', '''Aab-e-Kausar'', ''Rud-e-Kausar'' and ''Mauj-e-Kausar'', a history of Muslim culture in South Asia, were written by:', '["Shibli Nomani", "Sheikh Muhammad Ikram", "Allama Iqbal", "Mir Taqi Mir"]', 1, 'S. M. Ikram''s Kausar trilogy traces Muslim religious and cultural history in the subcontinent.', '{"0": "Shibli wrote Seerat-un-Nabi.", "2": "Iqbal wrote poetry and lectures.", "3": "Mir was a poet."}'),
  ('PST-0304', 'Economy, resources and culture', 'Culture', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Economic Survey; Pakistan Studies (compulsory), PTB', 'The word ''Urdu'' comes from Turkish and means:', '["Army (camp)", "Poetry", "Language of the court", "Literature"]', 0, '''Ordu'' means army or camp; Urdu grew in military camps and bazaars.', '{"1": "It refers to an army camp.", "2": "The court language was Persian.", "3": "It refers to an army camp."}'),
  ('PST-0305', 'Economy, resources and culture', 'Sport', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Pakistan Cricket Board', 'Pakistan was given Test cricket status in:', '["1952", "1992", "1947", "1971"]', 0, 'Pakistan played its first Test, against India, in October 1952.', '{"1": "1992 is the year of the World Cup win.", "2": "Pakistan became a Test side a few years later.", "3": "1971 is the year of the first one-day international."}'),
  ('PST-0306', 'Economy, resources and culture', 'Sport', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question. HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) Part I, Pakistan Studies. Checked against: Ian Talbot, Pakistan: A New History; Pakistan Studies (compulsory), PTB', 'The first Pakistani to climb Mount Everest (2000) was:', '["Nazir Sabir", "Hassan Sadpara", "Ashraf Aman", "Samina Baig"]', 0, 'Nazir Sabir reached the summit of Everest on 17 May 2000.', '{"1": "He climbed Everest later, in 2011.", "2": "Ashraf Aman was the first Pakistani on K2 (1977).", "3": "Samina Baig was the first Pakistani woman on Everest (2013)."}')
